## Fixes found by walking the deployed Lakebase-free test app
================================================================================

Context:
The SQLite-registry build was deployed to a test workspace with no Lakebase
binding (DAB target dev) and walked headlessly (screenshots, browser console,
failed requests). The registry, the Volume snapshot and a restore after an app
restart all worked; three UI issues were found and fixed.

Changes:

1. src/front/routes/domain.py, src/front/templates/partials/domain/_domain_information.html
   With the SQLite registry the domain Backend tab disables the Lakebase card
   ("Not available: this workspace runs without Lakebase") and falls back to
   the route-supplied default backend (Lakehouse) instead of 'lakebase'.
2. src/front/static/config/js/settings-registry-configuration.js
   Check Access success toast says "UC and registry permissions" (no longer
   "Lakebase" whatever the backend).
3. src/front/templates/domain.html
   Load timed-task-log.js before query-sync.js; the domain page raised
   "TimedTaskLog is not defined" (backport of the 0.10.0 include).
4. app.yaml.template, scripts/deploy.config.sh
   Optional REGISTRY_SQLITE_SNAPSHOT_PATH (APP_REGISTRY_SQLITE_SNAPSHOT_PATH)
   pins the snapshot path; UC lowercases volume names, so the derived default
   can differ from the real path.
5. tests/units/front/test_kg_access_info.py
   Renders with the route-supplied default backend; new case for Lakehouse.

