## E2E harness: never send the live workspace bearer to third-party hosts
================================================================================

Context:
In live mode the e2e and scenario contexts carry `Authorization: Bearer <token>`
in `extra_http_headers`, which Playwright adds to every request, including CDN
sub-resources (the app loads D3 from jsdelivr). `_install_redirect_fix` only
routed app-host documents and let everything else through with the header, so
a real workspace OAuth token was sent to third-party hosts. Found before running
the scenario campaign against the SQLite-registry test instance.

Changes:

1. tests/e2e/conftest.py
   `_install_redirect_fix` adds a route for every URL outside the app base that
   re-sends the request without the `authorization` header.
2. tests/e2e/security/test_live_bearer_scope.py (new)
   Two local HTTP servers stand in for the app and a CDN; the CDN must receive
   no bearer. Fails on the previous harness, passes with the fix.

Modified files:
- tests/e2e/conftest.py
- tests/e2e/security/test_live_bearer_scope.py

Tests: `ONTOBRICKS_E2E_FAKE_CREDS=1 uv run --frozen pytest tests/e2e/security/test_live_bearer_scope.py`
-> 1 passed (and 1 failed against the previous harness).

================================================================================
## E2E harness: always mint a full-lifetime bearer for live runs
================================================================================

Context:
Running the scenario campaign against the SQLite-registry test app, scenario 1
lost its session mid-Auto-Map: from one minute to the next the Apps gateway
answered every call (including /health) with a 302 to login, without reaching
the app. The first token of a run came from the CLI cache and expired minutes
later, while a Playwright context keeps the bearer it was created with for the
whole (15+ minute) scenario.

Changes:

1. tests/e2e/conftest.py
   `_resolve_live_bearer` always mints with `--force-refresh`, so every token
   starts with its full lifetime (the 12-minute cache keeps refreshes rare).

Modified files:
- tests/e2e/conftest.py

Tests: live scenario campaign against the SQLite-registry test instance (see
the next section for results).

================================================================================
## Lakehouse graph reported as empty while its search cache is pending
================================================================================

Context:
The scenario validation flagged "V1 knowledge graph built: 0 triples" on a
Lakehouse (zero-copy) domain whose `…_graph` view held 2,318 rows. The domain
had `graph_cache_state = pending_refresh`, so the `…_entity_search` / `…_props`
companions did not exist yet. `get_status` probes only those companions (it
must not scan the pass-through graph view), so it returned 0 and
`/dtwin/sync/status` answered "Graph is empty". The same code is on 0.10.0
(`delta/ReadStore.py`).

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaFlatStore.py
   `get_status`: when the probe is the `…_entity_search` companion and it has no
   Delta detail (not built), fall back to a `LIMIT 1` on the `…_data` relation
   (`synced_table_name`). The graph view itself is still never queried.

2. tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_delta_status_probe.py
   New `test_graph_status_probes_data_when_search_cache_not_built`
   (red before the fix, green after).

Modified files:
- src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaFlatStore.py
- tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_delta_status_probe.py

Tests: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` -> 9756 passed, 339 skipped
(readiness-route test deselected: it retries a fake SQL host for ~15 min).

================================================================================
## SQLite registry: stop probing Lakebase for the registry row
================================================================================

Context:
The app log of the SQLite-registry test instance showed, at startup and then
about once a minute (when the 60 s negative cache expires), a Lakebase
connection pool being created and two failed project/branch host lookups.
`RegistryCfg.from_domain` reads the UC triplet from the Lakebase `registries`
row before falling back to the Volume binding, regardless of the registry
backend. It failed soft, but cost failing workspace API calls on page renders
and logged a misleading "Created Lakebase connection pool" INFO line.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/registry/RegistryCfg.py
   Extract Method `_lakebase_row_triplet`: returns None without touching
   Lakebase when `RegistryFactory.backend_name()` is not `lakebase`.
   `from_domain` shrinks from 127 to 120 lines.

2. tests/units/architecture/baseline.json
   Tightened the `RegistryCfg.from_domain` entry (127 -> 120).

3. tests/units/registry/test_registry_factory_backend.py
   New `test_sqlite_backend_never_looks_up_the_lakebase_row` (red before,
   green after).

Modified files:
- src/back/objects/registry/RegistryCfg.py
- tests/units/architecture/baseline.json
- tests/units/registry/test_registry_factory_backend.py

Tests: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` -> 9757 passed, 339 skipped
(readiness-route test deselected, as above).

