## SQLite registry: flag it in the UI as a fallback mode
================================================================================

Context:
The SQLite registry exists only so OntoBricks can run where Lakebase is not
available (a customer region without Lakebase). The UI showed the SQLite mode
but never said it was a fallback or why, so it read like a nominal option.

Changes:

1. src/front/fastapi/dependencies.py
   New template global `registry_fallback()` (True when the registry backend is
   not Lakebase).

2. src/front/templates/base.html
   A "SQLite fallback" warning badge next to the registry icon in the navbar,
   with a tooltip that explains the mode and that it is not the target
   architecture.

3. src/front/templates/partials/registry/_registry_configuration.html
   A "Fallback mode" alert at the top of Settings > Registry.

4. src/front/templates/partials/domain/_domain_information.html
   The disabled Lakebase card says why: the registry runs in SQLite fallback
   mode until Lakebase is available.

5. src/shared/fastapi/health.py
   The SQLite registry check reads "ready (fallback mode: no Lakebase on this
   workspace)".

6. tests/units/front/test_registry_fallback_flag.py
   Badge, alert and health wording (red before, green after).

